# Source pin for pip-audit, the vulnerability scanner the dependency-audit action
# runs over a repository's requirements locks.
# This file lists only the top-level tool; the fully resolved, hash-pinned lock
# that pip actually installs is requirements-audit.txt (generated from this file).
#
# pip-audit gets its own lock rather than joining requirements.in because its
# closure (cyclonedx-python-lib, rich, requests, CacheControl, ...) is fairly
# large and no other action needs it. One tool, one lock.
#
# The lock generated from this file is itself audited: this repository's CI runs
# the dependency-audit action over every requirements*.txt it holds, this one
# included, so the scanner's own dependencies are covered by the same gate as
# everything else.
#
# Regenerating the lock (do this whenever the pin here changes):
#
#   uv pip compile --universal --python-version 3.11 --generate-hashes \
#       requirements-audit.in -o requirements-audit.txt
#
# That command keeps the versions already present in the lock, so on its own it
# only re-resolves what a changed pin in this file forces. Transitive releases
# published since the last run are left alone, including security fixes for
# packages nothing here pins directly. Add --upgrade to re-resolve the whole
# closure, or -P/--upgrade-package NAME to move one package and whatever it
# drags with it, which keeps a security bump to a reviewable diff.
#
# --universal + --python-version 3.11 make the lock a superset covering every
# interpreter the action runs under, so every marker-gated and platform-gated
# entry resolves under --require-hashes.
#
# The floor is 3.11, so the lock does not cover Python 3.10.
# A package whose newest release dropped 3.10 is locked at that release alone,
# not at two versions under complementary markers, which Dependabot's uv updater
# cannot move (see the uv entry in .github/dependabot.yml).
# Raise the floor again, and regenerate every lock, when packages start dropping
# 3.11.
pip-audit==2.10.1

# typing-extensions is pinned here, though only cyclonedx-python-lib needs it and
# only below Python 3.13. Without this line the lock carries it as
# `; python_full_version < '3.13'`, a marker Dependabot's uv parser drops, so
# Dependabot would never propose a bump to it. An unconditional pin locks it
# without the marker. Keep it in the python-direct group in .github/dependabot.yml.
# Drop this pin, and its entries in dependabot.yml, once nothing else in the
# lock requires typing-extensions; otherwise it keeps an unused package locked
# and bumped.
typing-extensions==4.16.0
